{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>For I am YHWH your healer.</b> He guides you on this path so that you will not come to illness — like a doctor who warns his friend: do not eat such-and-such food so that you will not come to sickness — only if you hearken, etc. — all the illness, etc. — for I am YHWH who warns you before you do anything that brings you to illness and pain, for transgression brings illness, as it is said: ״נד קציר ביום מחלה״, etc. And the commandment is a remedy for a person, as it is said: ״ולכל בשרו מרפא״. From Rabbi Yosef Kara. And all this is explained like ״ולרש אין כל״ — and ״לא יעיר כל חמתו״ — any thing of His wrath. And so here: any thing of the illness — you shall not put upon yourself."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The note's reading of לא תשים עליך treats the verse phrase לא אשים עליך as if addressed to Israel ('you shall not put upon yourself'); rendered as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:19.476444477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}